\documentclass{article}
\title{Adaptive Thresholds for Network Intrusion Detection}
\author{R. Kowalska}
\date{May 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Scoring}
Each flow receives an anomaly score from an isolation forest trained on the previous day.
The thresholds $\lambda$, $\mu$ and $\sigma control when an alert is raised,
and they are re-estimated every hour from the traffic observed so far.

Alerts that cross the highest threshold are escalated to an analyst immediately,
while marginal cases are aggregated into a hourly digest for later review.
\end{document}

